-- QuestLocFlavor (generado 2026-10-17): objetivos completos, con dialogos, solo para narrar.
_G.QuestLocFlavor = _G.QuestLocFlavor or {}
QuestLocFlavor[15] = {
[7500]={"A company of Dragon-clan warriors is encamped at the northern end of the Gravenwood, marching down from Enedwaith.","Into the Dragon's Maw","'Indeed, this is as I feared. These orders are directing the Dragon-clan to join with a company from the Ox-clan at the Mustering Tree, from where they will march south to Wulf's Cleft.\
\
'This is troubling, but useful information.'","One of the Dunlending captains might carry the orders Thurbald seeks.\
\
Thurbald has asked you to find a copy of the Draig-lûth's orders.","Thurbald is hiding to the south of Uvel-cadlus.\
\
You should bring the orders you found to Thurbald at once.","Órdenes recogidas","'Though the Dragon-clan has long been known to war with even their own countrymen, I fear this company is not here to stir trouble in Dunland. There have been Dunlending travellers going to and fro between Pren Gwydh and Tâl Methedras, and the Draig-lûth have ignored them.\
\
'Perhaps one of them carries orders from their chieftain, or a general of their forces -- if there are such ranks among these wild men. Would you enter their camp, Uvel-cadlus, and seek such orders among their captains?\
\
'It will be dangerous, but such information can only benefit our cause.'","Recoge las órdenes","'Did you find any orders?'","Bring the orders to Thurbald"},
[7501]={"'Finish any other business you have in the village. Then, we will head into the forest to find Shathur-munzu. Let us see if these 'demons' are real.'","The horse was spooked by your approach and ran deeper into the forest.\
\
You should find the missing horse again.","Baradal is slightly shaken by the sudden death of the horse.\
\
'We are not alone out here! There are deep claw marks in its hide! Be on guard! The poor horse. He loyally followed his master into danger and met an undeserved fate.\
\
'Wait... look at these tracks! I believe the demons feared by the Woodmen are simply wargs. We are more than capable of handling this threat. We should proceed to Shathur-munzu at once.'","Baradal is standing by in Arhaim.\
\
When you are ready to head into the wilds, you should speak to Baradal.","Shathur-munzu is somewhere west of Arhaim.\
\
You should start by following the path west from the village.","You have found a cart sitting by itself in the road","This must be all that remains of the man you sought","Into the Dusk","Baradal believes the owner of the cart may still be alive somewhere in the forest west of Arhaim.\
\
You should search for the cart's owner.","'This cart is mostly empty, and misses both horse and owner. Someone may have headed toward Shathur-munzu in search of dwarf-gold. These tracks seem fairly recent; perhaps the ones who made them are still alive. We should head into the forest and search for them.'","Follow the path west from Arhaim","The horse has been killed!","Find the cart's owner","Armed with the information you need, Baradal wishes to head into the wilds in search of the dwarf ruin Shathur-munzu.","'The size of this paw print is rather alarming. Was this left by the 'Shadow Hunter'? Weapons at the ready, ${PLAYER}.'","Baradal can be called to your side with Baradal's summoning horn.\
\
You should talk to Baradal about what just occurred.","The dead cart owner's horse may still be alive somewhere in the forest of Duskenvale.\
\
You should find the missing horse.","Find Shathur-munzu","Talk to Baradal","You have found a cart sitting by itself in the road.\
\
You should talk to Baradal about this.","Baradal can be called to your side with Baradal's summoning horn.\
\
You should talk to Baradal.","Shathur-munzu can be found west of Arhaim, in the wilds of Duskenvale.\
\
You should find Shathur-munzu.","Find the missing horse","The horse is startled and runs deeper into the forest","Baradal pauses, alarmed by something ahead","'We found him too late. Unfortunate, but he did not heed the warnings of the villagers. I have heard many tales of greed twisting the hearts of Men.\
\
'There must be some evidence nearby as to the identity of the 'demon' who did this. And perhaps the horse who pulled that cart is still alive.'","'Whenever you are ready, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[7502]={"Has recogido el saco de provisiones","Habla con Folkath en la Fosa Colmilluda","En la Fosa Colmilluda","El saco de provisiones de Oxi se encuentra en el suelo junto a él, en Jazârgund.\
\
Oxi te ha pedido que lleves un saco de provisiones importantes al puesto avanzado de enanos en la Fosa Colmilluda.","Folkath espera las provisiones en el campamento de la Fosa Colmilluda, al final del camino al este de Jazârgund.\
\
Oxi te ha pedido que lleves las provisiones importantes que ha recogido a Folkath en la Fosa Colmilluda.","'Hay más amenazas en Moria de lo que originalmente pensamos, mi ${PLAYERNAME:buen[m]|buena[f]} . Nos has ayudado a lidiar con los Uruk-hai y los trasgos aquí en el Camino de Durin, pero una amenaza completamente nueva amenaza con extenderse desde el este; los morrovals, un antiguo aliado de Morgoth.\
\
'Una gran tribu de morrovals ha tomado residencia en la Fosa Colmilluda. Folkath y algunos otros han acampado allí para lidiar con esta amenaza, pero necesitan urgentemente suministros. He preparado este saco de provisiones, lleva las provisiones a Folkath si estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para ayudar en su tarea.'","Recoge el saco de provisiones cerca de Oxi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Oxi te ha pedido que ayudes a un grupo de enanos que intentan obstaculizar a los morrovals en la Fosa Colmilluda, en el lado este del Camino de Durin.","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido, viajero.[m]|Bienvenida, viajera.[f]} Es un placer conocerte, .\
\
'Ah, veo que has traído provisiones de Oxi. Estaba profundamente preocupado de que pudiéramos quedar aislados de Jazârgund, pero parece que has llegado aquí sano y salvo. Muchas gracias.'"},
[7503]={"With the Haradrim assault coming any moment, Indir is worried that some of the townsfolk are still outside the bailey walls.","'They're all inside? This is a great relief. The stars only know how much time we have. Not even they, for the sky is blocked from all celestial light!\
\
'Thank you. Now, we must prepare ourselves for the Southrons' assault!'","Sent townsperson into the keep (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'There is much to do and there may be little time! I must work on securing our defences, but I fear some townsfolk are still outside the bailey walls. Would you go through Arnach and send them in here, to me?'","Send townsfolk into the keep (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Some people remain outside the keep, in the town of Arnach.\
\
You should gather the townsfolk outside the bailey walls and send them into the keep for their safety.","Into the Fold","Indir can be found within the walls of Arnach's keep.\
\
All the townsfolk of Arnach should now be gathered within the keep. You should return to Indir to tell him this has been done.","Talk to Indir"},
[7504]={"'${PLAYER}!\
\
'I did not expect to see you here in the trenches. A surprise, to be sure, but a welcome one!\
\
'We have held the line here for some time now, and I am pleased to report that the approach to Zarkul-sulûn remains safe... as safe as it can be in a time of war! Why have you come this way?'\
\
You tell Órug that Glóin has sent you on a mission to Ifbar-athrâkh.\
\
'Glóin has ordered you to the forward trenches? Then you'd best be on your way, my friend!\
\
'Keep your head down and do not let those terrible fumes take hold of you!'","'Have you brought orders from commander Glóin? Give them here!'\
\
Agnar unfurls Glóin's orders and begins to read them.\
\
'It is as I feared, my friends.'","Across the field of battle, the burning ruins of Zudramdân loom...","Find Agnar Brokentooth at Ifbar-athrâkh","Agnar Brokentooth can be found at Ifbar-athrâkh.\
\
You have found Agnar Brokentooth in Ifbar-athrâkh. You should deliver Glóin's orders to Agnar Brokentooth at once.","'Things do not go well, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'We thought to sail beneath the notice of Gorgar's forces on the field, but when we were beset by ballista-fire when we drew nearer to Gundabad.\
\
'Many of my kinsfolk were lost in the burning of their ships, and it is only by some chance of fate that ours was not lost as well.\
\
'We plan to return to Zarkul-sulûn and tend our wounds. I plan to rejoin the battle, but this time, it shall be on foot.'","As the War of Three Peaks overtakes Elderslade, Glóin has need of hale warriors to see the battle to its end.","Advance to the forward trenches","'I have nothing of note to report, ${PLAYER}, except that not once in all my years in Mordor have I seen a troll with two heads!\
\
'Shakal-atrâd is ours, and we have rallied to its defence. For the Gabil'akkâ!'","'Hail, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'The War of Three Peaks has begun, and we of the Gabil'akkâ have delved our trenches in answer to the Orcs of Gundabad. Indeed, the lines of battle are drawn in the very earth of Elderslade! \
\
We may have secured a foothold at Zarkul-sulûn, but it will take more than one victory to triumph against Gorgar the Ruthless. To that end, I have a mission for you.\
\
First, I ask that you gather reports from the dwarves Órug, Zhúdo, and Gárjan. I must know more of how our forces fare in the field, and I trust you to hear their words.\
\
'Second and of most import, I have sent three of Prince Durin's most trusted veterans of the Sixth War of Orcs and Dwarves to establish a forward command at Ifbar-athrâkh. You are to deliver these orders to Agnar Brokentooth and aid him and the others as best you can.\
\
'I trust you alone with this mission. Be swift!'","Agnar stands among several dwarves deep within Ifbar-athrâkh","Órug, Zhúdo, and Gárjan can be found in the trenches or on the battlefield in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
Glóin has sent you on a mission to join the forces of the Gabil'akkâ on the battlefield and receive reports from Órug, Zhúdo, and Gárjan before delivering his orders to Agnar Brokentooth at Ifbar-athrâkh.","Talk to Gárjan","Known as Ifbar-athrâkh, the Gabil'akkâ have erected a defensive trench within the stones of Elderslade","Talk to Órug","Hacia la Contienda","Deliver Glóin's order to Agnar Brokentooth at Ifbar-athrâkh","The forward trenches can be found to the south of the ruins of Zudramdân in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
You have received reports from Órug, Zhúdo, and Gárjan. You should continue on to the forward trenches and deliver Glóin's orders to Agnar Brokentooth in Ifbar-athrâkh.","Talk to Zhúdo","Ifbar-athrâkh can be found beneath the hillside to the south-east of the forward trenches.\
\
You have arrived at the forward trenches and should now seek out Agnar Brokentooth in Ifbar-athrâkh."},
[7505]={"Speak with Galâmka","'Aha! I am glad that you are so eager to help our cause!'\
\
Galâmka laughs.\
\
'As I have said, there are people from all over here. If you truly wish to help, I ask that you speak with them as they could use your help as well.'","Into the Furrows","Told Galâmka <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>","Galâmka has information on the current state of Urash Dâr.","Tell Galâmka <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, that you are not frightened and that you wish to help the people of Urash Dâr.","Speak with Galâmka now that he knows you are not too scared to help.","'All of Urash Dâr has been overrun by Orcs, and amongst them are these demons from Utug-bûr... a monstrous evil.\
\
'The people here could use all of the help that be can managed, but I assure you it is a dangerous undertaking. I would understand if you are too frightened to help.'","Tell Galâmka <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>"},
[7506]={"'Gandalf, we have both seen that shades walk in the fields, but that is not the reason I called you here.\
\
'I am sorry for what I have done! I was a fool to trust Saruman. Look at the destruction he has caused, and indeed I am partly responsible for the damage his machines have caused here in the Gladden Fields! And the trap into which you walked, all unawares... it was I that sent you into it! Will you ever forgive me for that, my old friend?\
\
'I wish to right these wrongs, Gandalf. And I will begin here in the Vales of Anduin!'","Talk to Radagast in the Gladden Fields","Varthmath and Gandalf can be found at the Beorninghús.\
\
You should talk to Varthmath and Gandalf.","Radagast can be found on the northern edge of the Gladden Fields.\
\
You should talk to Radagast in the Gladden Fields.","Travel to the Gladden Fields with Gandalf to meet with Radagast","'Do not bear the weight of it yourself, Radagast. Saruman deceived us all. I had hoped I could steer him from that path, but alas! It proved not to be.\
\
'${PLAYER}, I charge you with the investigation of the Gladdenmere. I will stay here and converse with my friend Radagast, for there is much about which we must speak.'","Talk to Gandalf in the Gladden Fields","Radagast has travelled to the Woodmen village of Hultvís and seeks your assistance with strange shadows that have appeared along the River Gladden. Many Woodmen have noticed an eerie gloom near the entrance to the Gladdenmere. They came to Radagast seeking answers, and you should speak with him in Hultvís as soon as you are able.","'Radagast has been quite busy lately, assisting both Elves and Woodmen with their various troubles in Eryn Lasgalen and in the Vales. I will speak with him at once, if you say he wishes it.'","Gandalf can be found on the northern edge of the Gladden Fields.\
\
You should talk to Gandalf in the Gladden Fields.","Varthmath can be found at the old dock in the south-east side of the Gladdenmere.\
\
You should talk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere.","Radagast has travelled to the Woodmen village of Hultvís, seeking your assistance with strange shadows lurking in the Gladden Fields.","'Hello there, ${PLAYER}! The path here was freed of the stones that blocked it, but now shades and strange shadows descend upon the valley! The Elves I met on my travels here wish to assist us. Very few have ever ventured to the old dwarf mine of Kidzul-kâlah. I say we learn all that we can of this place, and then return with our report for Grimbeorn.'","Radagast can be found on the northern edge of the Gladden Fields.\
\
You should travel to the Gladden Fields to meet with Radagast and Gandalf.","Radagast can be found at Hultvís.\
\
You should talk to Radagast.","'The Gladdenmere, you say? I thought the path to that vale was blocked by a rock slide, and we were better off for it; it is not a welcoming place. The old dwarf mine of Kidzul-kâlah stands there, they say, long-abandoned. Meet me on the mountain path that leads toward Kidzul-kâlah when you are able. There is an old dwarf-dock there where we can meet.'","Into the Gladdenmere","Talk to Radagast at Hultvís","Talk to Gandalf inside Grimbeorn's lodge","'${PLAYER}, dear friend, you have done much to help my home and those in my care among the Vales of Anduin. I need your help once more! Something seeps into the soil from the lake of Gladdenmere, and although I cannot tell what may be the cause, I can feel a deadly darkness all about it. The ruin of an old dwarf mine rests along the side of the lake, abandoned now for almost an age.\
\
'The Beorning Varthmath knows a fair amount about dwarf-made structures, and of course my old friend and ally Gandalf is sure to have an opinion on the subject... more than one, I daresay! Look for him at the Beorninghús. After you have sought out the both of them, meet me in the Gladden Fields. Very well? Very well!'","The two wizards embrace and are soon deep in conversation","Talk to Varthmath at the Beorninghús","Talk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere"},
[7513]={"Habla con Eywind en el Paso Alto","Hacia el Paso Alto","'Como si no tuviéramos ya bastante que manejar aquí, parece que algunos de los exploradores de Rivendel se han extraviado en algún punto al este de aquí, allá arriba, en el Paso Alto. Un par de ellos que pasaron hace unas semanas dijeron haber oído rumores de que un nuevo Gran Trasgo había surgido en la Ciudad de los Trasgos, y quisieron comprobar si era cierto... y meterlos en problemas si lo era.\
\
'¡Bah! Ya hay suficientes líos en estas montañas sin que un par de elfos alborotadores provoquen más, escúchame bien, pero de todos modos se fueron, y no hemos sabido nada de ellos desde entonces. Uno de los míos fue con ellos —un sujeto llamado Eywind— así que deberían estar bien.\
\
'Ahora que lo pienso, Eywind también es un cabeza caliente. Se apuntó con los demás porque decía que encontraría más aventura allá arriba en el Paso Alto, según sus palabras... así que quizá sería buena idea que vayas a ver si están bien...'","Vighar Trotasendas te habló de un grupo de tres exploradores enviados desde Rivendel que pasaron por su campamento hace unas semanas para explorar las tierras orientales de las Montañas Nubladas, a medida que ascienden hacia el Paso Alto. Estos tres —los elfos Nogmeldir y Glorwen y el enano Eywind— tienen la misión de determinar la fuerza de la Ciudad de los Trasgos, donde se rumorea que un nuevo Gran Trasgo ha tomado el trono y podría estar preparándose para la guerra contra los asentamientos a ambos lados de las Montañas Nubladas.","Encuentra a Eywind y a sus compañeros en el Paso Alto, a través del paso que se extiende más allá de Pinnath Fenui y atraviesa Cirith Daur hacia el este.","'¡Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! ¿Qué trae por aquí a alguien como tú, entre los picos helados del Paso Alto?\
\
'¿Vighar te envía, dices? Buen tipo... pues resulta que estamos bien por aquí. Hay trasgos de sobra para entretenerse, y el clima no es tan malo, una vez que te acostumbras.\
\
'Ahora, sí tenemos un par de asuntos pendientes, si quieres llamarlo así... y parece que mi amigo flacucho ha perdido a su compañera. Glorwen llegó un poco antes que nosotros, y aunque dejó señales de haber llegado sana y salva, no hemos visto rastro de ella desde entonces. Es tranquilo, pero creo que empieza a preocuparse.'","'Deberías buscar a mi pariente Eywind allá arriba en el Paso Alto. Él y sus compañeros deben de estar acampados más allá de Pinnath Fenui, pasando por Cirith Daur.'"},
[7514]={"'Now how shall I go about this? False rumours first? Geographical? Alphabetical?'","'There you are. I have given Spall room to finish writing down his findings before he returns to the Lonely Mountain. I will send him back with an escort of my guards. I thank you looking after him, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'You are most welcome here. As I mentioned before, I fear no such storm as we weathered in battle, yet troubles have a way of creeping in, and lingering. An adventurer such as yourself could do much good among the simple smiths of the Iron Hills. If you remain and lend your hand, you shall be rewarded richly and gratefully.'","'...a most thorough survey of the foundations and supports...'","Investigated the Dwarves of Járnfast","'There you are! What a long stroll this was. Longer than I am accustomed to, I confess. Spall, I said to myself, you are a proud dwarf and you must not tire so easily. Still, I have rarely gone so far in one day!\
\
'Now then, we have work to do, do we not? One cannot see much from here, can one? Before we go on, however, let us review our task.\
\
'First, many rumours circled around the stair at Skald's Drop, on the Ironfold's south. We should visit there and see for ourselves. Second, at least as many rumours circle the Dalish town of Utterby, due east of here. Third and hopefully last, many were the rumours of Járnfast and of Lord Náin who sits within.\
\
'If we visit these three locations, we will have settled the majority of the claims.'","'There you are, ${PLAYER}. I must thank you for being my travelling companion on this expedition. I think - I think perhaps I shall get out more often.\
\
'Ah, but who are you trying to fool, Spall? You will go back to your scrolls and runes and objects of lore and forget the sky-topped lands.'","You should meet Spall the Lore-master in the Ironfold, which lies down the road that leads from the south-eastern gates of Dale.","Thorin stands before his throne in the court of Erebor.\
\
You should hear King Thorin's Stonehelm reply.","Talk to Spall","Investigated Utterby","King Thorin laughs unexpectedly.\
\
'Well, Spall! You have talked yourself nearly in a circle, between worthiness and unworthiness and worthiness again. You have made a fair point, however, that the Iron Hills may yet hold peril. Jangovar yet linger by the Long Lake to the south, after all.\
\
'I maintain that no dwarf in all the Lonely Mountain is more suited to this endeavour than you. However, perhaps what is called for is company. ${PLAYER}, would you do Erebor one more service, and go with Spall into the Ironfold? I dare say there is much there of interest for an adventurer like yourself.'","'Do see that Spall accomplishes his task safely, ${PLAYER}. And bear my greetings to my brother Náin in Járnfast, when you see him there.'","'As you may be aware, a plague of injudicious rumours have come into this court, nearly all concerning affairs in the Iron Hills.\
\
'In truth, we have heard little from my brother Náin in the month since the fighting ended, and I must grudgingly concede that a desire to hear how things go out there is reasonable, even if such wanton gossip is not.\
\
'Now, I have heard a very wise and reasonable suggestion from one of my trusted Lore-masters. And who better to act on such a sensible sooth than to dispatch its author into the Ironfold, where he can determine the truth of each and every rumour, then return here and set the record straight.\
\
'I am speaking of you Spall. You needn't look around as if it were someone else.'","'Hm... concerning the Jangovar upon the Ironfold...'","Into the Ironfold","Investigate the Dwarves of Járnfast","'We have done well and fully the task we were charged with, ${PLAYER}. Only, Lord Náin asked us to return to him once we were done. I will meet you there.'","You should talk to Spall the Lore-master.","Spall can be found before Thorin's throne in the court of Erebor.\
\
You should hear Spall's reply to King Thorin Stonehelm.","'We are in this together it seems. I must gather some effects both here and down in Dale. Let us meet just where the road enters the Ironfold, then. If you leave Dale through the south-eastern gate, you will find the way.'","Talk to Lord Náin again","'Let us see then... first, the stair at Skald's Drop, which lies along the southern edge of the Ironfold. Second, the Dalish town of Utterby right in the middle of the Ironfold. Third, eastward built into the Hills, Járnfast where Lord Náin sits.'","'Mm - me? Well, in truth, I did make just such a suggestion to ${PLAYER} here, for I abhor these rumours just as you do, my lord. I cannot deny that, no matter my humility.\
\
'And I will stand by what I have said. You should dispatch some dwarf keen of eye and stout of frame, fair of mind and with a good memory. And while many of those attributes this Lore-master would humbly claim to possess, surely King Thorin, you cannot mean to send me out there. I am no adventurer, or guard, or soldier.\
\
'If half the rumours whispered in this court are true - and indeed, more than half would be most contradictory and impossible - then the Ironfold might be a truly dangerous place!'","Investigate Skald's Drop","You should talk to Lord Náin again, at his seat in Járnfast in the Iron Hills.","Skald's Drop lies along the southern edge of the Ironfold, Utterby right in the middle, and Járnfast at its eastern edge.\
\
You should investigate the rumours about the Iron Hills near the stair at Skald's Drop, in the Dalish town of Utterby, and at the keep of Járnfast where Lord Náin dwells.\
\
If you get separated from Spall, use the horn to call him back.","Talk to King Thorin","Meet Spall in the Ironfold","King Thorin has charged Spall with visiting the Iron Hills to determine whether any of the rumours in his court are the least bit true.","Investigate Járnfast's foundations","Investigate Utterby","Skald's Drop investigated","Use this to call Spall back to you","Spall returns to your side, looking somewhat disoriented"},
[7515]={"'Yes, the ground shook here. Many of us were in the midst of battle. When our foes fell back, we turned homeward fearing the worst. To our great relief, Járnfast still stood. It was days more before Lord Náin's face was seen. And how he has changed! We stood in awe of him before. Now... well, I will say no more. Have you seen him for yourself?'","'If we have been quiet, it is because we have been hard at work repairing, reforging, and clearing the dust from our home. Yet we have ever been quieter and more industrious than our kin to the west.'","Now that you have talked to many dwarves in Járnfast, you should talk once more to Spall.","Into the Ironfold: Dwarves of Járnfast","'So there are rumours in my brother's court?'\
\
A wry smile shows in the one living eye in Náin's face.\
\
'There are rumours in Járnfast as well, I am certain, though a stern rebuke would meet the dwarf who brought them before me. It is a symptom of the quiet that follows the storm, no doubt, that many fear more storm. \
\
'But I think we will have no more storms, not such as we have weathered, though other troubles may come to us, from other directions.\
\
'But I wander in my thought. I grant you full leave to satisfy your curiosities. Or have you already done so? I would speak with you when your errand is at an end.'","'It was good to see my kinfolk, but better still to hear their voices, hearty and hale. I will return to Erebor with more news than just the task with which I was charged.'","The Dwarves of Járnfast will be able to confirm or deny the remaining rumours about the Iron Hills.","You should talk to the Dwarves of Járnfast, including Lord Náin.","Talk to Spall","'I heard that a dragon had returned to Erebor, and that Jangovar roam freely through Dale, which burns both night and day. Is any of it true?'\
\
When you tell the dwarf it is not, his face darkens for a moment, then brightens again.\
\
'Then my cousins are well. I am happy to hear it!'","Talk to dwarves in Járnfast (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'My kin in Járnfast will set to rest any rumours that remain. We must not forget to bear King Thorin's greetings to his brother Náin.'","'We should not attend only to the stonework while in Járnfast, ${PLAYER}. Good dwarves, kinfolk of mine, still dwell here, too - I hope!\
\
'They will settle any last rumours we have been charged to test. Not only that, but I shall be glad to see the faces of my kin.\
\
'Let us not forget, as well, King Thorin specially bade us bring his greeting to his brother Náin.'"},
[7516]={"You should talk to Spall about the foundations of Járnfast.","Now that you have inspected a great number of the cracks apparent in Járnfast's stonework, you should talk to Spall.","'Járnfast! This much we can say without any inspection: it has not been shaken to the ground. To be proper record-keepers, however, we must get closer and inspect any cracks in the stone from without and from within.'","Inspect cracks around Járnfast (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Inspected cracks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Investigate the rumours about the structural integrity of Járnfast.","Into the Ironfold: Foundations of Járnfast","'Many of the flaws in Járnfast's stone are older than you or I, ${PLAYER}, though a few are clearly new. Stone-masonry is among the lore I have studied in my days, and I can state with good authority that there is no fear of Járnfast tumbling today, or in a hundred years, barring some fresh calamity.'","You should examine cracks in the stonework of Járnfast, both inside and out.","Talk to Spall","Investigate the foundations of Járnfast"},
[7517]={"Collected water-skins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Into the Ironfold: Skald's Drop","You should return the axe to the strange dwarves at their camp-site near Skald's Drop. You should also ask them why the axe was tied to an ox.","You should view the Stair in the cliff's edge, at Skald's Drop in the Ironfold.","'And what of that ox your axe was tied to? What of that, I should like to know? Did that belong to you? And how, now that I think of it, did your belongings become scattered in the first place?'","Talk to Okuz","'The axe? Where is the axe? Ah, Túmo, you drak. You did not tell me that ran off, too. And how many thousands of leagues have we lugged that piece of iron?\
\
'Ah, kízinek, this is a very sour thing to have lost. If you can return to us our axe, you will be owed a debt, I assure you.\
\
'It ran off that way, across the river to I know not where.'","Collected large parcels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect water-skins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Spall","Find the axe","'What do you want?'\
\
The dwarf eyes you suspiciously.\
\
'I don't have to tell you anything. And besides, I have not time. As you can see, our possessions have become scattered - here, there, all about.'\
\
The dwarf stands, waiting for you to move on. When you do not, he shakes his head.\
\
'First, kízinek, help us, then talk. There - the small bags, the big parcels, the water-skins.'","The possessions are scattered near to Skald's Drop in the Ironfold.\
\
You should help the strange dwarves gather their scattered possessions, including small sacks, big parcels, and water-skins.","You should talk to Spall about the rumours regarding Skald's Drop.","You should talk to Spall, now that you have seen the Stair at Skald's Drop.","'Look, Túmo! The kízinek has brought us back your axe. I told you it was a terrible idea to -'\
\
The dwarf looks up at you and falls silent.\
\
'You wish to know who we are? We are dwarves, just like your friend here. Only he is - what is that word? -  Longbeard, while we are Zhélruka. Many thousands of leagues, as I have said to you, we have come from our home. Our home - it is no home. It is Dôm Fálesh.'","Bring the axe to Okuz and Túmo","'We had better get right up to the cliff's edge and see whether or not the Stair has been broken.'","Strange-looking dwarves stand around the camp-fire.","You should talk to Spall and hear his thoughts on what you have found in the Ironfold.","'Can't you see I'm busy? Off with you.'","You should hear what Spall has to say in response to Okuz's claims.","Return to Okuz and Túmo","Okuz and Túmo stand by their camp-fire, near Skald's Drop in the Ironfold.\
\
Hear Okuz's answer to Spall's charge.","You should talk to the strange dwarves you found at a camp-fire near to Skald's Drop in the Ironfold.","'It ran off that way, across the river to I know not where.'","Found an... ox?","Investigate Skald's Drop","'Well now, we have arrived at Skald's Drop. Properly speaking of course, the name refers to the cliff and, well, the drop. We had better get right up to it, enjoy the view, and see whether or not the Stair has been broken.'","'I suppose we'd better help them. Perhaps they'll be inclined to speak with us if we do.'","'Small bags, big parcels, water-skins - they are scattered all down there.'","Collect small sacks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected a small sack (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find the Stair","You should bring the belongings you gathered to Okuz and Túmo at their camp, near Skald's Drop.","You should look for a camp-fire inland near Skald's Drop, and see if there are any of the rumoured travellers there.","'You talk to them, ${PLAYER}. You are the adventurer, after all!'","Investigate the rumours about Skald's Drop and the Stair with Spall.","'It may not look it to you, but the Stair is as intact now as it was when last I came this way. Which... hm... I believe was the early days of my youth!\
\
'There is a fair stream of travellers coming from the Stair. What can we say of them? I do believe I espied the smoke of a camp-fire as we approached, earlier. Let us make our way back and find what there is to be found.'","'Well, if you ask me, there is little doubt that these dwarves attempted to saddle that ox with all they owned and ease the load upon their own two backs. No doubt it belonged to some Man or dwarf of the Ironfold, though after all the war this place has seen, who can say if its master yet lives.\
\
'My ire was up when I began my thoughts, ${PLAYER}, but on further reflection, the pathetic state of these dwarves, and the innocence of the crime, softens my heart.\
\
'They called themselves Zhélruka, and indeed this is a name known in lore, belonging to another proud line of dwarves. A line that has dealings with Durin's Folk in past times. I wonder what these two fled, and if others of their kin also come this way.'","'Am I much mistaken, or did he say their axe ran off toward the river?'","Found the Stair","'Túmo. What is this word - ox? No? We do not know it. We have never seen such a beast. We are poor and weary travellers. Many, many, many leagues we have gone on foot, and without our few possessions we would be done for.\
\
'Túmo and I, we thank you for helping recover them.'","You should search for Okuz and Túmo's axe, which they say 'ran' off away from their camp near Skald's Drop, toward the river.","Investigate the small camp","Talk to the strange dwarves","Collect larger parcels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[7518]={"Find signs of what happened","Investigate the rumours about the Dalish town of Utterby.","You should scout Utterby with Spall, making sure to get a view of the south and east gates, and looking out for signs of who controls the town now and how that came to pass.","'Though we cannot be sure without, as I said, marching straight into the lion's mouth, I fear the rumours we had heard in court hold some truth here. Jangovar tents at both gates, their flags raised and the Dalish ones thrown down? That is truly an ill sign carved in plain runes, if you ask me.'","Now that you have scouted the perimeter of Utterby, you should talk to Spall.","Investigate Utterby","'Behold, ${PLAYER}: Utterby, a trading town of the Dale-men. At least, that is what it had been before the battles upon the Ironfold. Viewed from a distance, one cannot help but suspect some of the rumours we have heard are true.\
\
'I am not a warrior and I have no desire to march into the lion's mouth, yet all the same, we must get a bit closer to be sure. Let us tour both the southern gate and the east gate, and see if we may learn who controls Utterby now, and how that has come to pass.'","Learn who controls Utterby now","View Utterby's east gate","View Utterby's south gate","Talk to Spall","Into the Ironfold: Utterby","You should talk to Spall about investigating the rumours regarding Utterby."},
[7519]={"You have entered Esh Mêkag via the escapees' secret route.\
\
You should talk to Ishûri in Esh Mêkag.\
\
If you need to re-enter Esh Mêkag, talk to Ishûri in Dur Nâgu.","Find Ebuzâm","Free Shakûl","You must help some prisoners escape Esh Mêkag before Ebuzâm will leave.\
\
You should rescue Ebuzâm's children, Enûtu and Shakûl, as well as the Aradûni soldiers and the kidnapped Beltáni.\
\
If you need to re-enter Esh Mêkag, talk to Ishûri in Dur Nâgu.","'Quickly, Ebuzâm needs medical attention. The others have gone ahead. Go through the tunnel, and we will return to our camp in the ruins.'","You have successfully rescued many prisoners from Esh Mêkag.\
\
You should report your success to Arâniz in Dur Nâgu.","Talk to Ishûri","You cut Ebuzâm free","'You... you are not one of the Ordâkhai. What is the meaning of this?'\
\
He appears to have been badly beaten, and left tied up in the muck as a form of punishment. You explain that you are here with Ishûri to rescue who you can from the prison.\
\
'Ishûri? She came back? That fool girl. If you say you are here to help, I will take your word for it, as I have little to lose. They plan on executing me tomorrow, either way. But I will not leave without my children. There are also two groups of newcomers that you should free, before the Ordâkhai can torture them to death.\
\
'Find them. I will wait with Ishûri.'","Use the tunnel to return to Dur Nâgu","Enûtu is free!","Talk to Arâniz","Free the kidnapped Beltáni","Ishûri has agreed to show you the secret way into Esh Mêkag.\
\
You should talk to Ishûri when you are ready to enter Esh Mêkag.","The kidnapped Beltáni are free!","You should find Ebuzâm somewhere in the Esh Mêkag pit-mine.\
\
If you need to re-enter Esh Mêkag, talk to Ishûri in Dur Nâgu.","Shakûl is free!","Free the captive Aradûni","You have rescued who you can.\
\
You should return to Dur Nâgu using the secret tunnel.","Free Enûtu","The captive Aradûni are free!","Arâniz believes you will need the escaped thralls' help to get into Esh Mêkag.\
\
You should talk to Ishûri and mention the name 'Ebuzâm'.","'The situation here is desperate. My men and many others are trapped inside, subject to unspeakable horrors. They force whoever they can capture to work, and those that will not work are tortured inside the keep until they will. I hear the prison's warden, Ratúlko the Bloody, is particularly sadistic in his approach....\
\
'The only path forward that I can see is careful infiltration. The escaped thralls must know of a secret way inside, but they are reluctant to tell me. They believe anyone who makes it inside will surely be caught and killed, or worse.\
\
'I have heard them mention someone called Ebuzâm with great respect. I think he helped them escape and is still inside. Talk to Ishûri, and see if you can convince her that if we can get you inside, you can help get their friend out.'","You ask Ishûri if she will show you the secret way into Esh Mêkag to rescue those inside. She recoils in horror.\
\
'You want to go INSIDE? No! No, you must not! Only a few of us have ever made it out alive... and those left behind are punished! They will torture you to death if they catch you! I can't in good conscience let you go in there!'\
\
You say you can rescue Ebuzâm if she shows you the way inside. She seems shocked that you know the name.\
\
'Ebuzâm? I... we owe him our lives. If you say you will free him, I must trust that you will.'","'You have done it! I thought I would never see them again... not alive....\
\
'Ishûri told me there were many prisoners missing from the mine. I fear the worst for them. Ebuzâm should know more. He will want to speak to you.'","Arâniz believes the only way to rescue the captured soldiers is to convince the escaped thralls to help you infiltrate Esh Mêkag.","'This is the pit-mine inside Esh Mêkag. This section is usually less-guarded than the others, but... something is wrong. There are fewer guards and working thralls than I would have expected at this time of day....\
\
'Here, keep this on. This Ordâkhai uniform allowed my escape. It should allow you to walk around unbothered. Find Ebuzâm, but don't draw too much attention! He will know what to do.'","Into the Jaws","'I will show you the way. Please, you must find Ebuzâm!'","Talk to Ishûri to enter Esh Mêkag"},
[7520]={"Spalvi está en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.","Habla con Spalvi en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación","'Por favor, no me molestes ahora. ¡Estoy ocupado trabajando! Si sigues derrotando enemigos aquí en Katûb-zahar, ¡esto llevará menos tiempo!'","Decides mantener los ojos bien abiertos por si ves a Bingo mientras ayudas a Ketill","'¡Muchas gracias, mi amigo tan servicial! Siento haberte hecho esperar un rato, pero hacer un mapa requiere tiempo, ¡y si te apresuras lo echas a perder!\
\
'El siguiente lugar que esperaba terminar de cartografiar es una biblioteca al noreste de aquí llamada Katûb-zahar. ¿Lucharás contra los enemigos que encontremos dentro mientras yo trabajo?'","'¿Estás dispuesto a ayudarme a cartografiar la biblioteca de Katûb-zahar, al noreste? ¡Perfecto!'","Spalvi ha accedido a reunirse contigo en la entrada al reino de los enanos de Moria, una vez que la Guarnición de Hierro haya abierto las Puertas de Durin, en la Puerta de Acebeda.","'¿Sí? ¿Estás interesado en mis mapas? ¡Perfecto, perfecto! ¡Siempre es un placer conocer a otro entusiasta! Hay mucho arte involucrado en dibujar mapas precisos, y te sorprendería lo poca gente que de verdad aprecia el esfuerzo!\
\
'Solo entre tú y yo, creo que al resto de la Guarnición de Hierro le importarían más mis mapas si incluyera en ellos la ubicación de vetas preciosas y depósitos de mineral, ¡pero eso no tendría lugar en estos mapas! Quizá haga un segundo conjunto de mapas más adelante. Pero por ahora estos mapas son únicamente para salas, cámaras, túneles y cavernas. Como cartógrafo, es importante concentrar tu enfoque y mantenerlo.\
\
'Estoy centrado en hacer mapas, y por lo tanto soy menos capaz en combate. ¿Me ayudarás a derrotar enemigos en el siguiente lugar que necesito cartografiar? Mientras tú luchas, yo dibujaré, y de ese modo nos ayudaremos mucho el uno al otro. ¡Gazatmur está al este de aquí!'","'¡No puedo creer que me encuentre aquí, ${PLAYER}, al pie de los grandes escalones dentro de Khazad-dûm! ¡La vista me deja sin aliento!'\
\
El buen ojo de Spalvi brilla de asombro.\
\
'¡Skorgrím hablaba de recuperar la gloria de los enanos, pero siempre decía que fueron los Elfos quienes nos la arrebataron! Ahora veo que nuestra gloria no fue realmente tomada, sino que simplemente se perdió durante un tiempo. ¡Ha permanecido aquí, bajo las montañas, para que la encontráramos de nuevo!\
\
'¡No puedo agradecerte a ti y a Bingo lo suficiente por cruzaros en mi camino, ${PLAYER}, o nunca habría visto estos salones! ¡Busquemos a nuestro amigo perdido! Los enanos de aquí hablan de un cartógrafo llamado Ketill que trabaja en un lugar llamado el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, al este. ¡Él conoce todos los entresijos de la exploración de Khazad-dûm!'","Decides regresar con Spalvi en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación y ver qué ha averiguado","Completa 'Volumen II, Libro 1: Los Muros de Moria' hablando con Ráthwald, cerca de Echad Dúnann y completando su cadena de misiones","Spalvi Corazonrecio está en el Umbral de Durin, justo en la entrada occidental a Moria.\
\
Spalvi ha decidido que seguir a la Guarnición de Hierro dentro de Moria es tu mejor esperanza de encontrar a Bingo Boffin.","Ketill el Cartógrafo se encuentra en la cornisa más alta, en medio de la biblioteca de Katûb-zahar, al noreste del Mirador de la Gran Excavación","Spalvi Corazonrecio ha decidido que no hay otra manera, y si deseas encontrar a Bingo de nuevo, tendrás que seguir a la Guarnición de Hierro dentro de Moria.","Hacia la Larga Oscuridad","'Durante nuestro estancia aquí, he sabido que la Guarnición de Hierro viajó hacia el sureste, a las ruinas de Echad Dúnann, fuera de la Puerta de Acebeda. ¡Deberías hablar con los enanos que están allí y ver si han conseguido acceder a Khazad-dûm! Si ya lo han hecho, o cuando lo hagan, ¡me reuniré contigo en la entrada del gran reino de los Enanos!'","'No es imposible creer que tu Bingo pudiera haber caído en un río subterráneo y haber sido arrastrado hasta Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Poco probable, quizá, ¡pero parece que nuestro amigo también lo es! Seguiré estudiando los mapas que tengo disponibles y te avisaré si descubro algún posible escondite para ese hobbit tuyo, amigo mío. ¡Es lo menos que puedo hacer!'","Habla con Ketill el Cartógrafo en lo alto de Katûb-zahar","Ketill el Cartógrafo está en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, situado en Moria.\
\
Spalvi ha oído que un enano de la Guarnición de Hierro llamado Ketill está haciendo mapas de Khazad-dûm y podría ayudarte a encontrar a Bingo.","Habla con Spalvi en el Umbral de Durin, en la Gran Excavación de Moria","'Durante nuestro tiempo aquí, he sabido que la Guarnición de Hierro viajó hacia el sureste, a las ruinas de Echad Dúnann, fuera de la Puerta de Acebeda. Deberías hablar con los enanos que están allí y ver si han logrado acceder a Khazad-dûm. ¡Si ya lo han hecho, o cuando lo consigan, me reuniré contigo dentro de la entrada al gran reino enano!'","Derrota enemigos en Katûb-zahar hasta que Ketill termine de trabajar en su mapa","'¡Terminado! ¡Gracias por tu ayuda! Ahora que tengo algo de tiempo para pensar, ¿por qué no me dices qué es lo que buscas en estos salones?'\
\
Le cuentas a Ketill una versión abreviada de la aventura que provocó tu separación de Bingo. El enano piensa durante un momento.\
\
'No es imposible creer que pudiera haber caído en un río subterráneo y haber sido arrastrado hasta Khazad-dûm, ${PLAYER}. Poco probable, quizá, pero parece que nuestro amigo también lo es! Seguiré estudiando los mapas que tengo disponibles y te avisaré si descubro algún posible escondite para ese hobbit tuyo, amigo mío. ¡Es lo menos que puedo hacer!'","Ketill el Cartógrafo se encuentra encaramado en un muro en lo alto de Gazatmur, al este del Mirador de la Gran Excavación.","'Los enanos de aquí hablan de un cartógrafo llamado Ketill, que trabaja en un lugar llamado el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, al este. ¡Él conoce todos los secretos de la exploración de Khazad-dûm!'","'Por favor, no me molestes ahora. ¡Estoy ocupado trabajando! ¡Si sigues derrotando enemigos en Gazatmur esto llevará menos tiempo!'","'Esperaba que no tuviéramos que seguir a los Barbiluengos a Moria, ${PLAYER}. Puede que ya no sea un Duramano, pero los viejos resentimientos no se desvanecen tan fácilmente. Bueno, si no me reciben con acero, yo les responderé con amabilidad, ¡y no de la misma manera!\
\
'Durante nuestro tiempo aquí, he sabido que la Guarnición de Hierro viajó hacia el sureste, a las ruinas de Echad Dúnann, fuera de la Puerta de Acebeda. ¡Deberías hablar con los enanos que están allí y ver si han conseguido acceder a Khazad-dûm! Si ya lo han hecho, o cuando lo hagan, ¡me reuniré contigo dentro de la entrada al gran reino enano!'","Ketill el Cartógrafo te ha pedido que combatas enemigos en Katûb-zahar, al noreste del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, hasta que haya terminado su trabajo.","'Hemos empezado con buen pie, amigo mío. Ketill el Cartógrafo quizá encuentre alguna idea de lugares en los que podamos buscar a Bingo, y yo enmendaré el daño que causé cuando era un Duramano. ¡Estoy seguro de que está cerca!\
\
'Willem Bigotes no permaneció mucho tiempo aquí en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación. ¡Él también está buscando a Bingo! Sé que encontraremos a nuestro hobbit desaparecido, y confío en que será pronto!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Bert Bartolín ha llegado al Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La próxima semana: 'Willem toma la delantera' (Nivel Recomendado: 53)</rgb>","Ketill el Cartógrafo te ha pedido que derrotes enemigos en Gazatmur, al este del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, hasta que termine su trabajo.","Habla con Ketill el Cartógrafo en lo alto de Gazatmur, al este del Mirador de la Gran Excavación","Derrota enemigos en Gazatmur hasta que Ketill termine de trabajar en su mapa.","Habla con Ketill el Cartógrafo en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación"},
[7521]={"Thane Sparhafoc is in the Mead Hall, in the eastern part of Fenmarch.\
\
Guthláf asked you to inform his father, Thane Sparhafoc, about the troubles at the lumber-yard.","'It's so calm and beautiful here.'","Talk to Thane Sparhafoc","'Allow me to worry about the lumber-yard, ${PLAYER}. I ask that you travel to Fenmarch and inform my father of what has happened here.\
\
'If these Orcs were also seen near Aldburg, I fear that we may have a much larger problem than we originally thought.\
\
'Take the road east to Fenmarch and seek out my father, Thane Sparhafoc.'","Into the Marsh","Travel to Fenmarch","'You assisted my son in driving the Orcs from the lumber-yard? Thank you.\
\
'It appears that we have a problem which needs solving. There are other pressing matters here in Fenmarch which I struggle with.\
\
'Perhaps you may assist me?'","Thane Sparhafoc is at Fenmarch, east of the lumber-yard.\
\
Guthláf stayed behind to assist in the cleaning efforts at the lumber yard, but asked to have a message relayed to his father, Thane Sparhafoc.","The lumber-yard has been saved, but the Orc-problem remains a growing concern."},
[7528]={"Wights defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Meet Mêshaget at the entrance to Lâkindar","'Explain yourselves! Why is my grandson injured, and why is he in my hall instead of my hale-house?'\
\
Châmelek Gêta appears to be furious. Mêshaget hobbles forward and kneels before her, holding out the journal of Semayâti the Unyielding. She snatches it out of his hands and looks it over, flipping through the pages before she pauses, and her look of anger is replaced with one of wonder.\
\
'What is this?'\
\
Humble, and without looking up, Mêshaget says, 'The designs of Semayâti the Unyielding, that we may use to build defences to protect Jiret-menêsh and its people.'\
\
She sets the book aside as Mêshaget returns to his feet.\
\
'You fools went into the Quelling-house!? Did I not tell you that this place is forbidden? Tell me why you disobey me, Mêshaget!'","Complete Instance: Into the Quelling-house","'I am relieved you came!'","Châmelek Gêta is at once furious with you both but also awestruck at having the journal of Semayâti the Unyielding handed to her. She demands Mêshaget explain what this is about. You should talk to Mêshaget.","Mêshaget promised to explain what is going on when you meet at the top of the great staircase at Lâkindar's entrance. Lâkindar is located far to the south of Jiret-menêsh in An Shêru.","Talk to Mêshaget","'That went better than I expected, ${PLAYER}! Châmelek Gêta may be stone-headed, but she is not blind to reason when it is in front of her. Jiret-menêsh has a bright future ahead, and she will soon see that.\
\
'Thank you for all the help you have given me. You are a steadfast friend, and you came at the right time for when I truly needed one. Sâdikiz crafted his own fate, which I know in my mind, but my heart hurts for what I have done, regardless.\
\
'Should I have shown him mercy? I do not think he would have shown me any, but does that make my wrath warranted? Was a death blow truly necessary? It will be some time before I can sleep easily at night, I think.\
\
'I wish you the best on your travels, ${PLAYER}. May we meet again in more prosperous times.'","Following a confrontation with Sâdikiz the Sky-hungry and his Ordâkhai allies, you have helped an injured Mêshaget return to Jiret-menêsh where you were both immediately brought before an angry Châmelek Gêta.","'Châmelek Gêta, you are wise, and only want what is best for all of us. That, I understand and respect. I was not unaware of what lurks within the Quelling-house, and I chose to enter this forbidden place, risking my own life, for the chance to bring safety to our people without sacrificing their freedom.\
\
'I do not believe that things must be only one way or the other. We can have both security and freedom if we fight for it! Barkhûsh and his priests are gone. Ordâkh has no Hûl... or perhaps too many Hûls, I am not sure. By all accounts, they should be weakened! We can surely defend ourselves against them, and can do so with allies, if only we allowed ourselves to make some.\
\
'If Zajâna were to find value in trading with us, they would likely be willing to help defend us, should it become necessary. Evil does not lurk in the hearts of all Men. It was Men who killed the Hûl in Gondor, and it is said that the same Men helped bring Barkhûsh to his knees. And what of the Shoreward Stone? As Temámir, we are not friendless or alone.\
\
'I only ask that you examine the works of Semayâti the Unyielding, and allow for further discussion.'\
\
Mêshaget bows to the Gêta respectfully as he ends his argument.","Find the entrance to the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding","Talk to Mêshaget outside of Lâkindar","Unsurprisingly, the Dead here are not at rest","Mêshaget has pleaded his case with Châmelek Gêta as well as he could, asking only that she take the time to review the journal and consider the option of making alliances and fortifying the city. You should talk to Châmelek Gêta to hear her response.","You have cleared a path in the Quelling-house and have yet to see Mêshaget. You should search for the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding.","You have travelled to Lâkindar and found Mêshaget waiting for you. You should talk to him.","Into the Quelling-house","Mêshaget wants to ensure neither of you were followed here. You should enter the Quelling-house and assess the situation.","'${PLAYER}, when you met Sâdikiz, what was your opinion of him? Did you think him honourable? It pains me to question the motivations of one I have long considered a mentor and friend, but since we have succeeded in opening the gates, he has started asking many questions he should not. He seems to have no ill will for the hall of his fathers, but I cannot help but wonder now if it was all a lie. A false face to earn my trust and then use me to the ruin of our people.'\
\
The young dwarf looks thoughtful for a moment.\
\
'There is something I must do, and I wonder if you would help me. To the south lies the ruin of Lâkindar. Many refer to it now as The Quelling-house. Lâkindar was once a wealthy mine of the Temámir, but many years ago, the priests of Barkhûsh turned it into a slaughter-house and sacrificed many innocent people there, Man and dwarf alike, to their wicked deity. As you may imagine, Châmelek Gêta has forbidden us from going there. The place is surely cursed.\
\
'But go there I must. Would you accompany me? I will tell you more of our purpose once we arrive. Meet me at the top of the great stair. You will know it when you see it.'","Derrota a los tumularios (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Disturbed by something in Sâdikiz's letter, Mêshaget has decided that he must enter Lâkindar, the Quelling-house, and he has asked you to accompany him.","'I am relieved you came! This place has a foul air. It strikes fear in my heart and makes my hair stand on end! I do not think I could enter were I alone.'\
\
Mêshaget is sweating, visibly afraid of this place and is fighting to gather his courage.\
\
'It is said that inside Lâkindar lies the tomb of a legend, Semayâti the Unyielding. At the time of Lâkindar's height, she was a celebrated Temámir crafter, inventor, and engineer. It is said that there was nothing she could not do well!\
\
'It is believed that upon her passing, she was entombed with her journal, which was filled with many inventions and designs that were never made into reality. According to the history I have read, one of these designs was a plan to fortify Jiret-menêsh against attackers.\
\
'We have been relying on secrecy and ignorance to protect ourselves for one hundred years, ${PLAYER}. It is only a matter of time before those who envy our great wealth decide to take it for themselves, and our lives with it. We will find the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding and recover her journal. I will convince Châmelek Gêta to make these designs a reality so that we may live as part of the world, and yet also live without fear.\
\
'Please go in ahead of me. I should remain behind for a few minutes to ensure neither of us has been followed, and then I will catch up to you inside.'","After a moment of silence, Châmelek Gêta responds.\
\
'It will be as you say. I will look upon what is in this book, and we will discuss your proposal. You have not won, Shakâr-inik, I only agree to a discussion!'\
\
She leans forward conspiratorially.\
\
'Speak to me, ${PLAYER}, do you have children? Grandchildren? If not, avoid it at all costs! I fear that as Mêshaget comes into his own, he is becoming more stubborn than I am! One day, he will be Gêta and may do as he wills. Why he is impatient and chooses to spend all of his time fighting with me, I will never know.\
\
'There is a part of me that wishes to punish you for allowing him to endanger himself on such an unwise adventure, but I do not think you would have been able to talk him out of it if you had tried. Instead, I suspect that you are the only reason the fool is still alive. Am I correct?\
\
'Thank you for returning my rough gem to me. I am glad he has you for a friend.'","As you approached what you thought was the entrance to the tomb of Semayâti the Unyielding, you heard a frightened scream from inside. It must be Mêshaget! You should enter the tomb and help him.","Enter the Quelling-house","The dead have awoken and are roaming the halls of Lâkindar. You should defeat some of the wights to clear the way for Mêshaget.","This looks like the tomb entrance","Talk to Châmelek Gêta","Châmelek Gêta agreed to examine the plans in the journal and discuss the situation with Mêshaget after she has done so. You should talk to Mêshaget inside the Gêta's hall.","Instance: Into the Quelling-house completed"},
[7529]={"Arohir ha oído que los buenos hijos de la tierra de Ram Dúath están acosados por enemigos de Angmar, y te ha enviado a investigar.","'Por favor, busca al señor de los hijos de la tierra en el oeste de Ram Dúath.'","En el Ram Dúath","'¿Vienes de parte de Arohir, pequeño? Sí, conozco ese nombre desde hace tiempo. Cuando vinimos a este lugar hace muchos años desde el sur, él dio la bienvenida a nuestro pueblo y nos ofreció regalos en señal de amistad.'","El señor de los hijos de la tierra está en su aldea en el lado oeste de Ram Dúath.\
\
Arohir te ha enviado con los hijos de la tierra de Ram Dúath para ofrecer ayuda contra las fuerzas de Angmar que los acosan.","'He oído que los hijos de la tierra en Ram Dúath están acosados por enemigos de Angmar. Tenemos pocas fuerzas para ayudarles, con el ejército orco a nuestras puertas, pero si quieres, quizá puedas ir a ayudarles.\
\
'Los hijos de la tierra tienen una aldea en el lado oeste de Ram Dúath. El lado este está fuertemente controlado por Angmar, así que deberías evitarlo por ahora. También deberías evitar las guaridas de los dragonzuelos que anidan aún más al oeste que los hijos de la tierra. Busca al líder de los hijos de la tierra y háblale en mi nombre.'"},
[7530]={"Glorfindel está cerca del Bruinen en Rivendel.\
\
Faimir sugiere que hables con Glorfindel y descubras qué es lo que le preocupa.","'Deberías hablar inmediatamente con el señor Glorfindel.'","'Iorelen fue una vez miembro de mi compañía. ¿Podrás encontrarlo y hablar con él sobre los peligros en Núrz Ghâshu?'","'Si Glorfindel confía en ti, yo también pondré mi confianza en ti.'","'¿Has hablado con Faimir? Es amable de su parte preocuparse, pero no hay nada que pueda hacer.\
\
'Un amigo mío, Iorelen, se aventuró en Angmar hasta la Falla, un lugar que los sirvientes del Enemigo llaman Nûrz Ghâshu. Se dice que un gran mal habita allí bajo las Montañas de Angmar, y él fue a buscar noticias sobre ello. Glathlírel, otro aliado mío, fue allí hace mucho tiempo y no regresó, aunque se dice entre los Sabios que el mal allí fue contenido.\
\
'Quizás puedas ser de ayuda. Has viajado a Angmar, ¿verdad? Quizás puedas llegar al campamento de Iorelen, lejos al noreste en la tierra de Angmar, y averiguar el destino de Glathlírel.'","Glorfindel está preocupado por los eventos recientes y el recuerdo de un mal mayor en Angmar.","'He oído rumores de que Iorelen sigue vivo y se encontraría lejos al norte y al este, en Angmar.'","Iorelen se encuentra en el campamento de Iorelen, lejos al noreste en Angmar.\
\
Glorfindel te pidió que buscaras a Iorelen y averiguar si todavía vive.","'¿Glorfindel te envió? En efecto, la Sombra de Angmar llega incluso hasta aquí, a la Grieta de Nûrz Ghâshu. Es bueno que hayas venido, pues necesitaremos ayuda para repeler la Sombra.'","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Has llegado en un momento muy oportuno. ¿Has hablado con el señor Glorfindel? Parece preocupado últimamente, pero no quiere hablar de ello.\
\
'¿Lo conoces bien, verdad? Quizás te revele sus preocupaciones. Si puedes, ve a hablar con él cerca del Bruinen.'","Al interior de la Falla"},
[7531]={"'Habla con Ymar, Moggi, Pentlenn y Glorelloth y pregúntales qué hay que hacer en las Excavaciones Tenebrosas. Cuando hayas completado sus encargos, informaré a Veúlfur de toda la ayuda que nos has brindado aquí en el Refugio Sombrío.'","'Saludos. He estado esperando tu llegada desde que vi por primera vez a los demás hablando contigo en el Refugio Sombrío. No pareces tener mucho miedo de este lugar, pero sí el respeto necesario para saber que aquí nada es seguro. También veo que no dejas que la oscuridad afecte tu corazón, y eso me hace sonreír.\
\
'Estoy aquí a petición de Veúlfur, que está asignado a la Sala Vigesimoprimera, y he estado observando cómo intentas descubrir el secreto de la plaga que portan los orcos. Yo también busco ese secreto.\
\
'Hay otros cuatro a los que he pedido que me ayuden. Te pido que hables con ellos, aquí en el Refugio Sombrío, antes de adentrarte en las Excavaciones Tenebrosas para descubrir qué secretos pueden esconder. Ymar, Moggi, Pentlenn y Glorelloth necesitarán de tu ayuda. Por favor, habla con ellos.'","Habla con Gelirwen en el Refugio Sombrío","Gelirwen se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío.\
\
Has completado todas las tareas que te encargaron Moggi, Ymar, Glorelloth y Pentlenn, y debes volver con Gelirwen para darle la noticia.","Recupera las runas de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas para Pentlenn","Descubre el secreto de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas para Glorelloth","Ayuda a Moggi a eliminar a las criaturas terribles que habitan en la oscuridad de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas","Ayuda a Ymar a expulsar a los gusanos luminiscentes de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas","En las profundidades más oscuras de Moria, hay un lugar donde la única luz que brillaba provenía de las lámparas de enanos y hongos luminiscentes. Ahora estos túneles son más tenues que nunca y hogar de criaturas que existen solo en pesadillas. Sin embargo, ahí están, y los agentes de Veúlfur enviados al Refugio Sombrío encuentran poco consuelo al saber que hay algo en las Excavaciones Tenebrosas que ordena a los orcos a envenenarse de una manera que los entrega a una voluntad superior.","Completa la misión que te han encargado Ymar, Moggi, Pentlenn y Glorelloth en los alrededores de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas y luego regresa con Gelirwen.\
\
Gelirwen desea saber qué secretos pueden ofrecer las salas más oscuras de Moria a la expedición al Refugio Sombrío.","'Enviaré un mensaje a Veúlfur y compartiré contigo un gran conocimiento que me han transmitido aquellos a quienes ayudaste.\
\
'El Gurvand al que te enfrentaste en las Excavaciones Tenebrosas no fue el causante de esta plaga. No, fue obra de otro, y aún desconocemos la identidad de esa criatura. Su malicia no conoce límites, y tendremos que permanecer alerta ante cualquier indicio de que se esté acercando cada vez más a la superficie.\
\
'Te damos las gracias por tu ayuda en este descubrimiento.'","Hacia la oscuridad salvaje"},
[7532]={"Talk to Felgúr","'Felgúr continued on while you were searching the camp. Fear not, I did not lose track of him. He is at the top of the Winding Stair. It is from there we will enter Torech Ungol.\
\
'I am wary of travelling together up the stair. If these Bloodless Uruks have set up an ambush, that is where they will attempt it. We will be in the open and without footing. I will stay back and cover you. Go on and find Felgúr.'","Celeborn can be found outside Torech Ungol.\
\
You should talk to Celeborn.","'They are near. I can smell them. I smell HIM. The Pale Herald.'","Celeborn and Legolas are outside Torech Ungol, at the top of the Winding Stair.\
\
You should talk to Celeborn and Legolas.","The time has come to enter Torech Ungol, confront Rûkhor the Pale Herald, and discover if Shelob yet lives.","Help Celeborn with 'Caging the Spiders'","You quickly inform Mablung of all you learned in Kaslokroz and of what occurred in Torech Ungol. Mablung looks both distressed and awe-inspired.\
\
'Wait, wait, hold a moment! Let me see if I have this right. Rûkhor wants to rouse the wounded Shelob from her lair so she eats everyone and everything, and when she goes back to sleep he wants to take Mordor for himself. That is a terrible, terrible plan! And, not only that, but he convinced the Ungoledain to lead him right to her, and he gave Felgúr back his skin-changing? Then that poor fool went after Shelob, she ATE him, and almost ate you as well, but Celeborn, the Lord of Lórien himself, stepped in to save you?'\
\
You nod and confirm that is the summary of what transpired. He takes a moment to steady himself.\
\
'What a day, ${PLAYER}. What a day. I will send for reinforcements at once and move all available scouts to keep watch on Torech Ungol. No one will come or go without our knowledge. When Celeborn is ready to confront Shelob, we will stand with him.'","Talk to Mablung","Celeborn has asked you to swiftly return to the rangers in Echad Taerdrim.\
\
You should return to the rangers and talk to Mablung.\
\
Speak to Legolas to return there quickly.","Into the Spider's Den","'Lord Celeborn speaks true. The Rangers must be made aware of what transpired here. Let us return to Mablung as swiftly as we are able.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will swiftly travel to Echad Taerdrim!</rgb>","Celeborn has asked for your help containing the spiders in Torech Ungol.\
\
You should help Celeborn with 'Re-forming the Snare' and 'Caging the Spiders'.","Help Celeborn with 'Re-forming the Snare'","'They are coming. I hope you are ready for a fight.'","'You must tell me everything, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
You tell Legolas of Rûkhor giving Felgúr back his skin-changing, the encounter with Shelob, and Rûkhor's final taunt. Legolas takes a moment to carefully consider everything.\
\
'I believe his plan was to use Felgúr and yourself to lure Shelob out. He knew you would try to run, and perhaps she would follow you out of Torech Ungol into the Morgul Vale. But, he could not have anticipated Celeborn's appearance.\
\
'Yes... I believe it is Rûkhor's aim to rouse Shelob from her underground lair so she may devour all in her path. His enemies, and his rivals. As ever, this all distills down to the former servants of the Dark Lord squabbling for control of his fading empire....'","'It has been some time since my last encounter with Ungwetári. Time has only made her more dangerous, more ravenous. Her wound has only increased her aggression and inflamed her hatred. We must do what we can to contain her and the Gúrzyul Rûkhor. To do nothing is to allow calamity.'","Felgúr has continued ahead to Torech Ungol, and is waiting at the top of the Winding Stair.\
\
You should climb the Winding Stair and find Felgúr.","Complete 'Instance: She Who Walks in the Darkness'","'Our efforts will hold the spider-horde in Torech Ungol, for now. Soon we must pursue Ungwetári herself, but until then I ask you and Legolas to return to the Rangers of Ithilien and inform them of Rûkhor's plot. We will soon need a small force to enter the deep tunnels: Remmorchant, the Net of Darkness. That is where we will meet the spider-queen. That is where I will end this. I will send for you when the time is right.'","Felgúr has tracked his people to the top of the Winding Stair.\
\
You should talk to Felgúr, and be ready for a fight.","Habla con Celeborn","Habla con Legolas."},
[7533]={"El árbol furioso se encuentra en el camino del norte del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Habla con el árbol furioso.","Con la esperanza de reunir provisiones para reparar su pueblo devastado, los habitantes de Puente de Caballetes han abierto las puertas del Bosque Salvaje. Sin embargo, el bosque es peligroso y el camino está bloqueado.","'Bueno, ${RACE}. ¿Has venido tú también a despojar a estas tierras de sus riquezas?'.\
\
Le explicas la difícil situación de los habitantes de Puente de Caballetes.\
\
'Hmmm, hoom. Creo que puede haber una forma de que trabajemos juntos en beneficio tanto del Bosque Salvaje como de Puente de Caballetes, ta-rum.'","En el Bosque Salvaje","'Saludos. Te doy la bienvenida al Bosque Salvaje, donde hasta los árboles caminan, hablan y se niegan a dejarte pasar. Pareces de los que les gusta la aventura. Quizá puedas echar una mano. Hay un árbol muy enfadado bloqueando el camino hacia el Bosque Salvaje.\
\
'Quizá puedas hacerle entrar en razón, aunque siento que he perdido la cabeza. Mi abuela solía contar historias de árboles andantes en estos bosques. Nunca pensé que vería uno. Mi mujer insiste en que es un troll del bosque, pero... tú pareces capaz de valerte por tu cuenta.'","Habla con el árbol furioso"},
[7534]={"Walt Rosablanca está acampado en las ruinas en el extremo occidental del lago conocido como Nen Harn.\
\
Gil Hojarena te pidió que hablaras con Walt Rosablanca sobre la extraña cosa que vio al norte del bosque de Chet.","'¿Gil Hojarena dice qué? Bueno, no voy a negar que el Bosque Viejo es un lugar extraño -- y no importa lo que te diga la gente, los árboles se mueven -- pero nunca he oído hablar de algo así en el bosque de Chet.\
\
'Aun así, si Gil te envió aquí para hablar conmigo, entonces es justo pensar que él mismo tuvo un gran susto.'","En el bosque","Los bosques de las Tierras de Bree pueden ser oscuros y misteriosos. Algunos lugares son más oscuros que otros....","'Bueno, ¿qué te dijo Walt?'","Habla con Walt Rosablanca en Nen Harn","'Juro que lo vi, aunque mis vecinos dicen que estoy loco. Estaba en el extremo norte del bosque de Chet, cerca de Nen Harn, todo solo por supuesto, y vi algo moviéndose entre los árboles.\
\
'No, no es del todo correcto. Me pareció que los propios árboles se estaban moviendo. Algo grande y terrible está en el bosque, y tengo miedo de lo que podría ser.\
\
'Hay un grupo de cazadores que acampa en el extremo occidental de Nen Harn, estaba allí entregando la sopa de pez globo de la señora y me perdí un poco -- fue entonces cuando lo vi. Cuando los encontré, les conté lo que vi, y me pregunto si podrías preguntarle a Walt Rosablanca si ha visto lo mismo?'"},
[7535]={"Looks like Corsairs got to the workers first","Haelam is short-handed and could use some help tracking down his workers up in the woods.","The workers can be found in the forest south of Tadrent, in the foothills of the Emyn Ernil, above the beacon Nendath.\
\
You should find the workers there and help them finish their task.","Bring the wood back to Haelam in Tadrent","Build crate (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Decent workmanship, for an adventurer. Now, shouldn't you be out there taking care of those Corsairs?'","Examine one of the bodies","The workbench is located near Haelam in Tadrent.\
\
Use the workbench to build crates for Haelam.","Haelam is located in the village of Tadrent.\
\
Speak with Haelam.","Search for the missing workers","Crates built (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The workers' camp-site can be found in the forest south of Tadrent, in the foothills of the Emyn Ernil, above the beacon Nendath.\
\
You should examine a body and collect wood for Haelam.","Haelam is located in the village of Tadrent.\
\
Bring the wood back to Haelam in the village of Tadrent.","'These crates are falling apart and we very much need some new ones. Just before you arrived I sent a couple of my workers up to the forest to fetch some wood. The troubling thing is that they haven't returned. Most likely, they took the day off!\
\
'Could you go up to the forest and find them, ${PLAYER}? While you're at it, bring back some wood and tell those two they don't work for me any more!'","'Dead?! These Corsairs are ruining everything! This will be the end of my business!'\
\
Haelam calms down a little.\
\
'While you're here, could you finish the job you started and make me a couple new crates?'","This is indeed one of Haelam's workers","Speak with Haelam","En el bosque","Collect wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[7536]={"You have found Shúkurz and Phocas outside Kafagur, near the northern side.\
\
You should talk to Phocas.","The trail continues north out of Kafagur","'Thanks for making sure I was all right, ${PLAYER}. Grúshul's right; I acted like a fool. Even during our journey out of Gundabad, we stuck to the wilds because we knew Men would kill us if they saw us. I should have been scared of Phocas.\
\
'But... I remembered how we got out of Gundabad in the first place. With your help, and the help of others. I remembered Náin, and how he apologized to me.\
\
'I guess I wanted to believe that sort of thing could happen again. Maybe it can.'","Follow the trail of footprints out of Kafagur","Shúkurz has abandoned all caution to try and reason with a strange Man.","Shúkurz has left behind a trail of footprints leading out of the northern side of Kafagur.\
\
You should follow it.","Talk to Shúkurz","Intrepid Hope","Talk to Phocas","'I am sorry, ${CLASS}; I followed you from Mâr Naphra to find Kafagur. I had believed that it was a camp full of dangerous Orcs. Clearly, I was mistaken, and this investigation was faulty from the start.\
\
'It's true that I am not from Umbar, but rather, Gondor. I... do not know if I can tell you what led me here, but you have my word: I will not harm the Orcs.\
\
'Whether they believe me is another matter entirely. Though, after I judged them so rashly, I do not know if I deserve that trust.'","'Phocas doesn't seem like the bad sort. After all, he was willing to stop running long enough to listen to me. I'm sure we'll figure things out.\
\
'I've got more I want to tell you, but I ought to take Phocas back to Kafagur first. I'll see you there.'","Shúkurz has asked you to talk to him back in Kafagur.","'No matter how much I'd like to send more guards after Shúkurz, it'd only make things worse with that Man. But you're different; I'm sure he's the kind who'd trust you over an Orc.\
\
'It won't be hard for you to track down Shúkurz. See that trail of footprints, leading out of the village? Heh, I bet he was a lousy scout in Gundabad.'","You have found Shúkurz and Phocas outside Kafagur, near the northern side.\
\
You should talk to Shúkurz.","Upon noticing you, Phocas looks down in shame","Talk to Shúkurz in Kafagur"},
[7537]={"'Golpea al muñeco de entrenamiento con tu nueva habilidad y vuelve a mí. Debemos asegurarnos de que estés ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para enfrentarte a los peligros de la Tierra Media.'\
\
PISTA:\
\
Los Capitanes dependen de su <rgb=#00ff00>Grito de Batalla</rgb> para entrar en un <rgb=#ffff00>Estado de Preparación para la Batalla</rgb>. Mientras estén en este estado, los Capitanes pueden usar habilidades especiales como <rgb=#00ff00>Golpe devastador</rgb>, un ataque efectivo que inflige gran daño. Ataca al <rgb=#ff0000>Muñeco de Entrenamiento</rgb> con tu <rgb=#00FF00>Grito de Batalla</rgb> para ponerte en <rgb=#ffff00>Estado de Preparación para la Batalla</rgb> y luego ataca al muñeco con tu <rgb=#00ff00>Golpe devastador</rgb>.","Usa <rgb=#00ff00>Golpe devastador</rgb> sobre el muñeco de entrenamiento cercano. \
\
PISTA:\
\
Los Capitanes dependen de su <rgb=#00ff00>Grito de Batalla</rgb> para entrar en un <rgb=#ffff00>Estado de Preparación para la Batalla</rgb>. Mientras estén en este estado, los Capitanes pueden usar habilidades especiales como <rgb=#00ff00>Golpe devastador</rgb>, un ataque efectivo que inflige gran daño. Ataca al <rgb=#ff0000>Muñeco de Entrenamiento</rgb> con tu <rgb=#00FF00>Grito de Batalla</rgb> para ponerte en <rgb=#ffff00>Estado de Preparación para la Batalla</rgb> y luego ataca al muñeco con tu <rgb=#00ff00>Golpe devastador</rgb>.","El Instructor de Capitanes se encuentra en los campos de entrenamiento de Archet, muy cerca de la puerta.\
\
Ahora que has usado con éxito tu habilidad recién aprendida, deberías regresar con tu instructor y contarle tu éxito.","Has usado con éxito Golpe Devastador","'¡Te doy la bienvenida a Archet, ${PLAYERNAME:compañero Capitán[m]|compañera Capitana[f]}! Me especializo en enseñar a ${PLAYERNAME:guerreros[m]|guerreras[f]} como tú habilidades y destrezas útiles. Supongo que has venido con ese propósito, así que aquí tienes un consejo:\
\
'Recuerda, un Capitán no sirve mejor a sus compañeros corriendo imprudentemente al combate. No, es cuando se mantiene atrás y dirige los esfuerzos de sus compañeros que realmente brilla. Allí puede ver las debilidades de sus enemigos o impulsar a sus compañeros hacia adelante e inspirarlos a la victoria.\
\
'Demuestra tu habilidad usando <rgb=#00ff00>Golpe devastador</rgb>\
\
PISTA:\
\
Los Capitanes dependen de su <rgb=#00ff00>Grito de Batalla</rgb> para entrar en un <rgb=#ffff00>Estado de Preparación para la Batalla</rgb>. Mientras estén en este estado, los Capitanes pueden usar habilidades especiales como <rgb=#00ff00>Golpe devastador</rgb>, un ataque efectivo que inflige gran daño. Ataca el <rgb=#ff0000>Muñeco de Entrenamiento</rgb> con tu <rgb=#00ff00>Grito de Batalla</rgb> para ponerte en <rgb=#ffff00>Estado de Preparación para la Batalla</rgb> y luego ataca al muñeco con tu <rgb=#00ff00>Golpe Devastador</rgb>.","Usa tu <rgb=#00ff00>Grito de Batalla</rgb> sobre el muñeco de entrenamiento y luego golpéalo con tu habilidad <rgb=#00ff00>Golpe devastador</rgb>","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! A medida que crezcas, aprenderás habilidades adicionales. ¡Buena suerte!'","Habla con el Instructor de Capitanes en Archet","Tu instructor quiere que uses tus nuevas habilidades para demostrar que estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para enfrentar los muchos peligros que existen en el mundo.","Introducción: La Carga de un Capitán"},
[7538]={"Habla con el entrenador de Guardián en Edhelion","Dorongúr Espinablanca está en Edhelion.\
\
Debes ir a Dorongúr Espinablanca y decirle que has terminado tu meditación y que estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para la batalla.","'Sí, sentí que estabas bien ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}, . Recuerda, debemos trabajar para recuperar esta tierra y aunque tenemos una paz tentativa con los enanos en el valle, no podemos olvidar las lecciones del pasado y la traición que vino de sus manos.\
\
Habla con Dorongúr y dile que creo que estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}.'","'Me alegra saber que has completado tu meditación y entrenamiento. El camino por delante está lleno de desafíos, y todos debemos prepararnos para lo que está por venir. Creo que esta lección permanecerá contigo.'","Golpea el muñeco de entrenamiento con Barrido de Escudo","'Te enseñaré más cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para aprender. Por ahora, deberías hablar con Dorongúr.'","'Golpea el muñeco de entrenamiento con tu nueva habilidad, luego regresa conmigo. Debemos asegurarnos de que estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para enfrentar los peligros de la Tierra Media.'\
\
CONSEJO:\
\
Los Guardianes dependen de <rgb=#ffff00>Habilidades Reactivas</rgb> para causar daño y generar <rgb=#ff0000>Amenaza</rgb> contra sus enemigos. <rgb=#00ff00>Barrido de Escudo</rgb> requiere que el Guardián <rgb=#ffff00>Bloquee</rgb> un ataque enemigo antes de poder usar la habilidad. Dirígete a los <rgb=#ff0000>Muñecos de Entrenamiento</rgb> al norte del entrenador y atácalos hasta que bloquees uno de sus ataques. Si tienes problemas para bloquear, prueba usar <rgb=#00ff00>Resguardo del guardián</rgb> para aumentar tus posibilidades de bloquear ataques enemigos. Una vez que hayas bloqueado un ataque podrás usar tu habilidad <rgb=#00ff00>Barrido de Escudo</rgb>. Golpea el <rgb=#ff0000>Muñeco de Objetivo</rgb> con <rgb=#00ff00>Barrido de Escudo</rgb>.","Has golpeado el muñeco de entrenamiento con Barrido de Escudo","Habla de nuevo con el entrenador y aprende la habilidad <rgb=#00ff00>Barrido de Escudo</rgb>. Usa tu nueva habilidad en el muñeco de entrenamiento cercano.\
\
<rgb=#00ff00>NOTA: Usa el entrenador y selecciona Entrenar habilidades de Guardián para abrir el panel de selección de habilidades. Haz clic izquierdo en una habilidad para resaltarla y luego haz clic en el botón Entrenar en la parte inferior del panel de selección de habilidades, o haz doble clic en la habilidad, y comprarás la habilidad con éxito.</rgb>\
\
CONSEJO:\
\
Los Guardianes dependen de <rgb=#ffff00>Habilidades Reactivas</rgb> para causar daño y generar <rgb=#ff0000>Amenaza</rgb> contra sus enemigos. <rgb=#00ff00>Barrido de Escudo</rgb> requiere que el Guardián <rgb=#ffff00>Bloquee</rgb> un ataque enemigo antes de poder usar la habilidad. Dirígete a los <rgb=#ff0000>Muñecos de Entrenamiento</rgb> al norte del entrenador y atácalos hasta que bloquees uno de sus ataques. Si tienes problemas para bloquear, prueba usar <rgb=#00ff00>Resguardo del guardián</rgb> para aumentar tus posibilidades de bloquear ataques enemigos. Una vez que hayas bloqueado un ataque podrás usar tu habilidad <rgb=#00ff00>Barrido de Escudo</rgb>. Golpea el <rgb=#ff0000>Muñeco de Objetivo</rgb> con <rgb=#00ff00>Barrido de Escudo</rgb>.","Introducción: El Barrido de Escudo del Guardián","'Incluso en este refugio caído hay amenazas que debemos enfrentar. Sin el ojo atento y el cuidado de los Elfos, Edhelion se ha convertido en hogar de muchas criaturas antinaturales. Necesitarás saber cómo defenderte y derrotar estas amenazas.\
\
Debes aprender habilidades de otros, como yo. Podemos guiarte en tu entrenamiento y ayudarte a ser más fuerte.\
\
